          {
            "x": 2.178649237472767,
            "y": 12.910611231371064,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Post-Presidency</strong><br>\nAfter his presidency, Wałęsa remained active in politics and public life. He has been a vocal advocate for human rights and democracy. His opinions often spark debate, reflecting his ongoing commitment to Poland's political landscape.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Personal Life and Legacy</strong><br>\nWałęsa is married to Danuta Gołoś and they have eight children. His personal life is woven into his public persona, reflecting his role as a family man and leader. His legacy is marked by his transformation from an electrician to a world-renowned leader.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Wałęsa Today</strong><br>\nToday, Lech Wałęsa continues to speak about political issues in Poland and worldwide. He is often seen as a symbol of Poland's fight for freedom and democracy. Despite controversies that sometimes arise, Wałęsa's impact on Poland's history is undeniable.</p>\n"
              },
